# Nuxt 4 Frontend

- Use Composition API with `<script setup lang="ts">`.
- State: `useState` or typed Pinia stores. Prefer `shallowRef` for large non-reactive objects (terminals, log buffers).
- Styling: Tailwind utilities only - no inline styles.
- Types: strict TypeScript; define shared types in `~/types/`. Never use `any`.
- Validation: Zod for forms and API payloads.
- Real-time: prefer SSE or WebSockets for deployment logs; always remove listeners in `onUnmounted()`.
- **Reuse first**: before new UI, search `components/`, `composables/`, `utils/`. Prefer composing existing pieces over duplicating markup or fetch logic.
- **GitHub selection**: always use `GithubInstallationPicker` + `GithubRepoPicker` (and `~/utils/githubAccount`) for account/repo pickers. Do not rebuild `<select>` lists for installs or repos.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD - listener leak + any
onMounted(() => eventSource.addEventListener('message', (e: any) => { ... }))

// ✅ GOOD
const es = shallowRef<EventSource | null>(null)
onMounted(() => {
  es.value = new EventSource(url)
  es.value.addEventListener('message', onMessage)
})
onUnmounted(() => {
  es.value?.removeEventListener('message', onMessage)
  es.value?.close()
})
```

```vue
<!-- ❌ BAD: one-off install + repo selects -->
<select v-model="installationId">...</select>
<select v-model="repo">...</select>

<!-- ✅ GOOD: shared GitHub pickers -->
<GithubInstallationPicker v-model="installationId" :installations="installations" />
<GithubRepoPicker v-model="repoFullName" :installation-id="installationId" @select-repo="onSelect" />
```
